# Authentication Page Patterns

## Unified Auth Flow

The auth page at [src/app/auth/page.tsx](mdc:src/app/auth/page.tsx) handles both sign-in and registration in a single unified flow.

## Flow Steps

1. **Email Step**: User enters email
2. **Email Check**: System checks if email exists
3. **Password Step** (existing user): Sign in with password
4. **Register Step** (new user): Complete registration

## Role Locking from URL

The auth page supports role locking via URL parameters:

```typescript
// Attorney sign-up
/auth?role=attorney  // Locks role to ATTORNEY

// Client sign-up  
/auth?role=client    // Locks role to CUSTOMER

// No parameter
/auth                // User can select role
```

### Implementation

```typescript
useEffect(() => {
  const roleParam = searchParams.get('role')
  if (roleParam === 'attorney') {
    setRole('ATTORNEY')
    setIsRoleLocked(true)
  } else if (roleParam === 'client') {
    setRole('CUSTOMER')
    setIsRoleLocked(true)
  } else {
    setIsRoleLocked(false)
  }
}, [searchParams])
```

## Step Management

### Step Types

```typescript
type AuthStep = 'email' | 'password' | 'register'
```

### Navigation

```typescript
const goBack = () => {
  if (step === 'password' || step === 'register') {
    setStep('email')
    setUserInfo(null)
    setErrors({})
    
    // Restore locked role if applicable
    if (isRoleLocked) {
      const roleParam = searchParams.get('role')
      if (roleParam === 'attorney') {
        setRole('ATTORNEY')
      } else if (roleParam === 'client') {
        setRole('CUSTOMER')
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Role Validation for Existing Users

When checking email of existing users:

```typescript
const checkEmailExists = async () => {
  const data = await fetch('/api/auth/check-email', {
    method: 'POST',
    body: JSON.stringify({ email })
  }).then(res => res.json())

  if (data.exists && isRoleLocked) {
    // Verify role matches
    const expectedRole = role // From URL parameter
    const actualRole = data.user.role
    
    if (expectedRole !== actualRole) {
      // Mismatch - redirect to correct auth page
      toast({
        title: "Role Mismatch",
        description: `This account is registered as ${actualRoleText}. Please sign in from the appropriate page.`
      })
      
      setTimeout(() => {
        const correctRole = actualRole === 'ATTORNEY' ? 'attorney' : 'client'
        router.push(`/auth?role=${correctRole}`)
      }, 2000)
      
      return
    }
  }
}
```

## Dynamic Titles and Descriptions

```typescript
const getStepTitle = () => {
  switch (step) {
    case 'email':
      return 'Sign in to AI Law Wizard'
    case 'password':
      return `Welcome back, ${userInfo?.user?.name || 'there'}!`
    case 'register':
      return 'Create your account'
  }
}

const getStepDescription = () => {
  switch (step) {
    case 'email':
      if (isRoleLocked) {
        const roleText = role === 'ATTORNEY' ? 'Attorney' : 'Client'
        return `Enter your email address to get started as a ${roleText}`
      }
      return 'Enter your email address to sign in'
    case 'password':
      if (userInfo?.user?.role) {
        // Support both ATTORNEY and legacy LAWYER
        const roleText = userInfo.user.role === 'ATTORNEY' || userInfo.user.role === 'LAWYER' 
          ? 'Attorney' 
          : 'Client'
        return `Welcome back! You're signing in as a ${roleText}`
      }
      return 'Enter your password to continue'
    case 'register':
      const roleText = role === 'ATTORNEY' ? 'Attorney' : 'Client'
      return `Complete your ${roleText.toLowerCase()} account setup`
  }
}
```

